## Workspace

One file per source under claims/, one JSON object per line. Lines that
start with # are ignored.

{% for s in sources %}
- {{ s.source_id }}-claims.jsonl for {{ s.title }}
{% endfor %}

## Claim fields

- claim_id: {{ 'S01-C001' }} style, the prefix must match the file's source
- source_id: the source the claim came from
- claim_text: the claim restated in your own words, one claim only
- claim_type: one of fact, finding, recommendation, definition, metric, procedure
- topic_tags: a list of lowercase kebab case tags, at least one
- supporting_quote_location: a section or heading reference
- confidence_as_stated: one of high, medium, low, unstated
- depends_on: a list of claim ids this claim depends on, usually []
- source_excerpt: 15 to 300 characters copied exactly from the sentence that
  states the claim, leaving out footnote markers and link syntax

The source_excerpt is the one check light mode keeps. RESYNTH finds it in the
source, so a claim the source does not contain fails. Pick a phrase that
occurs once in the source.

## Check

Check one source with resynth check-claims {{ project }} S01, then run
resynth extract-verify {{ project }} and fix every reported problem.
